# Demo capture "timetrial" (tools/video/capture.sh timetrial): the same start as demo-boot (Start,
# the controls panel hidden, the opening), then title -> licence 1 -> Single Player -> Time Trials
# -> default character, kart and drift -> Mushroom Cup -> Luigi Circuit -> Ghosts -> "Race This
# Ghost" -> Start Race: OK, with autodrive armed (guest-memory.js): the player's own kart drives
# the race on the disc's staff ghost's recorded inputs (1:29.670, scripts/parity/rkg-info.py),
# read by the game frame by frame as it reads any ghost, with the Time Trial's camera and HUD and
# no ghost kart on the track. Marks: page, start, title, main-menu, ghosts, ok (the press that
# loads the race); the capture's perf.json adds race-loaded from the game's own log.
#
# Needs a licence in slot 1: the site's game folder seeds a save (tools/hosting/stage-game.sh
# --save rksys.dat; one exported from any run with the page's Export save button will do).
#
# Left click is A, and every press counts: one press too many or too few and the D-pad presses
# land on the wrong screens. A D-pad press is also lost when it arrives before a menu has slid in;
# the Single Player menu is the slowest (black for ~2 s, ready at ~5 s on an idle machine), so it
# gets 8 s.
mark page
waitstart 90000
mark start
wait 2500
eval document.getElementById('hide-controls').click()
# The title scene: the game's THP library announces itself as it starts (the first such line).
# Counting from Start instead put the route one press off whenever the boot took a little more or
# less time (the attract demo it meant to skip had not started yet).
waitlog 120 RVL_SDK - THP
mark title
wait 3000
# title -> Select License (licence 1 under the cursor) -> main menu
click 500 430
wait 3000
click 500 430
wait 4500
mark main-menu
# Single Player, then down to Time Trials
click 500 430
wait 8000
key ArrowDown 150
wait 1500
shot single-player
click 500 430
wait 4500
# character -> kart -> drift -> Mushroom Cup -> Luigi Circuit -> Ghosts screen
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 8000
mark ghosts
shot ghosts
# "Race This Ghost" (under the cursor) -> Start Race: OK, which writes the ghost into the race
# setup; autodrive moves it onto player 0 before the race loads.
click 500 430
wait 4500
eval window.__mkwGuest.autodrive('ghost')
mark ok
click 500 430
waitlog 10 \[autodrive\] ghost
# the race: about 9 s of flyover and countdown, then the ghost's 1:29.670 and the finish
wait 30000
wait 30000
wait 30000
wait 20000
mark end
wait 500
